/* S4 code motion: a dot product is not moved. Mesa's linker runs before the back end lowers fdot2 to fmul(v.y, 3.0) and ffma(v.x, 2.0, that), and can_move_alu_across_interp refuses the vector-sourced fdot2, so the whole product stays in the fragment shader (the vertex shader is the plain copy, every lane of v stored) where the same arithmetic written out, s4_motion_sum's, moves. Also the FMA with the constant factor 2.0 and the FAU constant 3.0 (pan_shc's record, tools/mali/testdata/pan_shc-out/s4_motion_dot.json). */
precision highp float; varying vec4 v; void main(){ gl_FragColor = vec4(dot(v.xy, vec2(2.0, 3.0)) * v.z, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0); }
